{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/511765-wtf-the-pack","id":511765,"title":"WtF: The Pack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-12T00:46:48-07:00","id":511765,"title":"WtF: The Pack","content":"What is it? People who asked in the MM notes got no answer (at least until i checked last time).<br /> <br /> So lets speculate!<br /> <br /> I hope it is a book with more focus on the internal crucible of packs.<br /> Ideas on how Uratha operate with handling pack business. Expanded information on Wolfblooded and the humans that are added to the pack and the roles they play.<br /> Also more info on how the pack handles the different roles within. Who is alpha, how to challenge alpha etc etc.<br /> Hopefully the book adds more flavour to some of the most important dynamics in the game that the players control.<br /> <br /> Or..<br /> Maybe its the new players guide?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T00:59:42-07:00","id":511789,"title":"","content":"Given that WtF 2e heavily implies (and Dark Eras outright states) that packs are basically violent gangs, I hope it at least partly explores how completely <i>fucked</i> the average werewolf's mentality is. A revival of the Trust system as an optional mechanic (originally from the Storyteller's Guide) would also be absolutely delicious. And give us more Tells for the Wolf-Blooded!<br /> <br /> <i>(I'm a little bit sad that we're not seeing a guide to the Tribes - the Pure included - as the first supplement, but we all know it's coming eventually).</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T01:25:00-07:00","id":511807,"title":"","content":"It's a surprise. We'll hear more as it gets closer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T01:51:07-07:00","id":511840,"title":"","content":"Packs have expanded immensely from what they were in 1e, and there's a lot of ground to cover. I imagine there will be exploration of how mortal kin live and hunt alongside the Uratha. Advice on how to run mixed packs, troupe play, and how a violent supernatural culture caught between two dimensions manages to remain cohesive would all be useful. Crossover stuff seems helpful too, especially with Beast on the way.<br /> <br /> I know I'd personally like to see Damnation City-style territorial rules, but that will likely be outside the scope of this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T03:30:12-07:00","id":511862,"title":"","content":"It's on the weekly list now? Let me just go update my signature...<br /> <br /> (As for why no answers, we generally default to letting Stew speak for his lines, and he's afk at the moment.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T03:41:59-07:00","id":511864,"title":"","content":"Indeed. All I can say for now is that I'm excited about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wonder if Stew's planning to do any blog entries for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:50:31-07:00","id":511932,"title":"","content":"Seems like a Blood of the Wolf kind of deal, IMO.<br /> <br /> It'll probably have stuff on irregular packmates, such as spirits, animals, claimed (for the cult-head Ghost Wolf/Bale Hound), and other supernatural denizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:55:22-07:00","id":512026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/511765-wtf-the-pack?p=511840#post511840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Packs have expanded immensely from what they were in 1e, and there's a lot of ground to cover. I imagine there will be exploration of how mortal kin live and hunt alongside the Uratha. Advice on how to run mixed packs, troupe play, and how a violent supernatural culture caught between two dimensions manages to remain cohesive would all be useful. Crossover stuff seems helpful too, especially with Beast on the way.<br /> <br /> I know I'd personally like to see Damnation City-style territorial rules, but that will likely be outside the scope of this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope there's info on how to run mixed packs. Adding wolf blooded to your pack is no problem, but we've had real issues adding any humans, cos you can't tell them what you're doing, why you're in charge and can't use any of your powers while they're in the room (otherwise lunacy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:37:32-07:00","id":512057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/511765-wtf-the-pack?p=512026#post512026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope there's info on how to run mixed packs. Adding wolf blooded to your pack is no problem, but we've had real issues adding any humans, cos you can't tell them what you're doing, why you're in charge and can't use any of your powers while they're in the room (otherwise lunacy)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Moon's Mad Love is for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would love to see a chapter on other supernatural creatures as pack members. What role might a Changeling play in a pack? How do you deal with one pack member being unable to go out during the day? How does a Thyrsus packmate's unique perspective on the Shadow color the rest of the pack's approach to maintaining their territory? What do you do when you've got a Sin-Eater and a Rahu with The Other as a personal Death Rage trigger in the same pack? That kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:53:34-07:00","id":512088,"title":"","content":"Probably something like Coteries, but for werewolves. I was hoping we'd get an antagonist book early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:25:17-07:00","id":512154,"title":"","content":"On one hand I am really excited that WtF is already getting its first supplement. On the other hand this does not seem to be the supplement I was hoping for. I will wait to hear a bit more about what exactly will be in the book.<br /> <br /> There are so many things that need to be expanded because the core book did not have enough space for them. Most antagonists, Lodges, tribes, packs, perhaps rules for &quot;elder&quot; werewolves. I guess you have to start somewhere.<br /> Could rules for Lodges be in this book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T13:40:48-07:00","id":512284,"title":"","content":"I'm with others on this being a suppliment for every day living and possibly territory ruling. Maybe also pack vs pack combat, similar to the stuff from war against the pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T14:25:50-07:00","id":512337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/511765-wtf-the-pack?p=511932#post511932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like a Blood of the Wolf kind of deal, IMO.<br /> <br /> It'll probably have stuff on irregular packmates, such as spirits, animals, claimed (for the cult-head Ghost Wolf/Bale Hound), and other supernatural denizens.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we got spirit packmates then I would take back everything I've ever said about WtF and start a chronicle immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T14:51:21-07:00","id":512348,"title":"","content":"We've already been told we get them, and the core book gives you personal totems and buddy spirits in the touchstone section. Even a spirit of your future self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T15:05:27-07:00","id":512359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/511765-wtf-the-pack?p=512337#post512337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we got spirit packmates then I would take back everything I've ever said about WtF and start a chronicle immediately.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fire-Touched are notorious for having many spiritual packmates. There would likely be a rite for this purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T22:01:41-07:00","id":512534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/511765-wtf-the-pack?p=512088#post512088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably something like Coteries, but for werewolves. I was hoping we'd get an antagonist book early.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf already has more antagonist books than most other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Chris